cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "NanoTCAD ViDES, ported to Python 3.13, NumPy 2.x and GCC 14"
message: >-
  This citation covers the compatibility PORT only. If you use
  NanoTCAD ViDES for scientific work, please cite the original
  authors, Gianluca Fiori and Giuseppe Iannaccone of the
  University of Pisa, as given under references below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Thatte
    given-names: Manish Jagdish
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-8050-1242"
    affiliation: maniTLab, Nashik, Maharashtra, India
    email: manish@manitlab.org
repository-code: "https://github.com/manishthatte/NanoTCAD_ViDES"
url: "http://vides.nanotcad.com/vides/"
abstract: >-
  A compatibility port of NanoTCAD ViDES, the self-consistent
  NEGF and Poisson solver for nanoscale device simulation
  developed by Gianluca Fiori and Giuseppe Iannaccone at the
  University of Pisa. The original targets Python 2.7 and the
  NumPy 1.x C API and does not build on current systems; this
  port updates the C extension to the Python 3 and NumPy 2.x
  APIs and to GCC 14, leaving the physics untouched. All
  scientific content is the work of the original authors.
keywords:
  - NEGF
  - TCAD
  - device simulation
  - quantum transport
  - Python 3 port
  - software preservation
license-url: "https://github.com/manishthatte/NanoTCAD_ViDES/blob/main/license.txt"
version: 1.0-py313
